# Cloudflare Workers static-assets headers.
#
# Cloudflare serves static assets with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0,
# must-revalidate` by default, which forces the browser to revalidate every
# asset (a 304 network round-trip) on every navigation — even the content-hashed
# files under _next/static that can never change without their filename changing.
# That default was adding ~2.8s per navigation (9 fonts / 749kB revalidating each
# time). Overriding it for _next/static/* only — those are the immutable,
# content-addressed build outputs (JS, CSS, next/font woff2/ttf under media/) —
# is safe: a real change produces a new filename, so a year-long immutable cache
# can never serve stale content. Deliberately NOT applied to other public assets
# (images, the pattern SVG) since those keep stable names across edits.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public,max-age=31536000,immutable

# Security basics for every static asset, including the Rise export under
# /training-content/. Worker-rendered pages get these (plus CSP) from
# next.config.ts headers(); static assets never pass through that. SAMEORIGIN
# keeps the Rise iframe working on our own training page while refusing to be
# framed by anyone else.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
